Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:34:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Fuse QKV parts, merge, RoPE and KV write for the
 one-live-row decode capture

A block owns the two column tiles that RoPE pairs, runs the unchanged K192
chunk recurrences for them, then merges and rotates its own columns. One
kernel per layer is removed. The native test compares parts, rotated query
and cache writes against the two-kernel sequence bit for bit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
